  "principles": [
    "Persistence is evidence of persistence, not admission, semantic currentness, authority, truth, consent, identity, relationship state, or phenomenology.",
    "State belongs inside the Vera control architecture, but state does not automatically become control authority.",
    "Raw provider rows are never directly injectable into inference; provider/state records cross typed adapters and Cohesion admission first.",
    "Currentness is resolver-owned and lineage/evidence-bound, never timestamp-owned.",
    "Requested effect is distinct from payload/proposition and is separately authority-gated.",
    "A producer may lower its own authority/effect ceiling but cannot self-mint externally rooted authority, provider trust, admission, or current-route status.",
    "Derived views and indexes have no independent authority.",
    "Domain transaction semantics remain domain-specific; a common header does not imply one universal table, transaction pattern, or lifecycle model.",
    "Technical runtime-state semantics are authored in vera; vera-control-plane pins, deploys, verifies, and qualifies exact source generations without redefining their semantics.",
    "Private historical payload stays in its canonical private/specialist source unless separately authorized for another persistence surface."
  ],
